[] 3. How exactly does one set some of the game options, such as naming the 
[] character, and the numberpad option? Is it something I'd type from a
[] UNIX prompt, before starting the game, of would it be a bunch of flags
[] I'd add to the end of the start command, ie
[]          prompt---> %nethack -option1 -option2 -option3
[] I have no clue, and I'm sick of being named e5w127. :)

for csh add this line (suitably modified) to your .login:

setenv NETHACKOPTIONS "name:Leonardo,time,dogname:Bytor,fruit:large pizza"

changes take effect at next login ... (similar stuff for sh)

or, if you only want to set your name try:

nethack -u Leonardo 

also, there's some general help obtainable from within the game using
the "?" command.

